{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/connector at 68c0f42fee192e24bc194ec262cad359e4784fd3 on request/github-connector-render. The outbound half: Render composes a pull request whose body names the governing request, the artifact and the exact head, and states that approval and merge happen in gitseq rather than on GitHub; Client.Open performs the delivery and reports the created number and URL as evidence, failing when GitHub refuses and when it accepts but returns nothing usable. The connector never ingests its own writing — a rendering opens with the marker, and a test renders then re-observes through the inbound half without producing an act. Writing runs behind the same charter check as reading, and every proposal field is required rather than inferred.","body":{"commit":"68c0f42fee192e24bc194ec262cad359e4784fd3","path":"internal/connector"}}